{"id": "tea:kalagnirudra-upanisad:1-2", "source": "src:kalagnirudra-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1-2"}, "paraphrase": "Sanatkumāra asks about the tripuṇḍra; Kālāgnirudra: take ash with the five brahma-mantras, apply with 'fire is ash…', 'mā nas toke' and 'tryāyuṣam' in three lines across the forehead, chest and shoulders.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:tripundra"], "teachers": ["tch:sanatkumara", "tch:kalagnirudra"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kalagnirudra-upanisad:2-three-lines", "source": "src:kalagnirudra-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2 (three lines)"}, "paraphrase": "The first line is the gārhapatya fire, the letter a, rajas, earth, the outer self, the power of action, the Ṛgveda, the morning pressing and Maheśvara; the second the dakṣiṇa fire, u, sattva, mid-space, the inner self, the power of will, the Yajurveda, midday and Sadāśiva; the third the āhavanīya fire, m, tamas, sky, the supreme self, the power of knowledge, the Sāmaveda, the third pressing and Mahādeva.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "sound-language"], "practices": ["prc:tripundra"], "concepts": ["cpt:omkara-matras"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kalagnirudra-upanisad:3", "source": "src:kalagnirudra-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "3"}, "paraphrase": "Whoever wears the tripuṇḍra — student, householder, forest-dweller or renouncer — is purified of all sins and attains union with Śiva.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "practices": ["prc:tripundra"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
